<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kouklia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kouklia is a village in the Paphos District of south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a>, built on the site of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palaepaphos">Palaepaphos</a>, Old Paphos, the capital of one of the ancient city-kingdoms of the island. Its sanctuary of Aphrodite was one of the most famous in the Greek world. Excavations have revealed the sanctuary, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bronze-age">Bronze Age</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a> tombs and the Persian siege mound of 498 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kouklia.jpg" alt="Kouklia" width="320" height="207" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Chris06 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:St_Luke%27s_Church,_Kouklia,_Cyprus_(03).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
